0.500 .. +5.875)","colourIndexBand":"IMPORTANT: the stored colour index is NOT Johnson B-V for most stars. AT-HYG`s `ci` column is the Tycho BT-VT colour for every row whose mag_src is T, which is the large majority. Measured against HYG v4.1`s Johnson B-V over 106,941 cross-matched stars, the offset is colour dependent: about +0.00 at B-V 0.0, +0.02 at 0.45, +0.08 at 0.75, +0.18 at 1.05, +0.26 at 1.35, +0.32 at 1.75 and +0.50 beyond 2.0 — i.e. red stars are stored noticeably redder than their Johnson B-V. The 165 stars flagged 0x80 were back-filled from HYG v4.1 and ARE Johnson B-V. A renderer mapping colour index to temperature should either apply a BT-VT to B-V transformation or accept that K and M stars render somewhat too red.","magnitudeBand":"The stored apparent magnitude is AT-HYG`s `mag`, which for mag_src=T rows is the Tycho/Hipparcos band rather than Johnson V. Median offset against HYG v4.1 Johnson V over 107,336 cross-matched stars is +0.074 mag, reaching about +0.37 for the brightest stars (Sirius is stored as -1.088; its Johnson V is -1.44). Brightness ORDERING is essentially preserved, so brightest-first sorting and magnitude cuts remain valid, but the number should be labelled an instrumental magnitude, not V.","absoluteMagnitude":"absmag = mag - 5 * (log10(sqrt(x*x + y*y + z*z)) - 1)   — not stored; derive it from the dequantized mag and the position","positionL0L1":"float32 parsecs, stored verbatim — no quantization applied","positionL2":"x_pc = x_i16 * shell.scale, where shell.scale = shell.radiusPc / 32767 and a star`s shell is the manifest entry whose [start, start + count) index range contains it","flags":{"bit0 (0x01)":"has-proper-name — AT-HYG `proper` column is non-empty","bit1 (0x02)":"has-exoplanet — host matched a NASA Exoplanet Archive pscomppars row","bit2 (0x04)":"is-variable — HYG v4.1 `var` (variable-star designation) is non-empty for the HIP/HD-matched row","bit3 (0x08)":"is-multiple — HYG v4.1 `base` non-empty or `comp` > 1 for the HIP/HD-matched row","bit4 (0x10)":"ci-was-defaulted — AT-HYG `ci` was empty; the stored value is the solar default 0.65","bit5 (0x20)":"has-bayer-or-flamsteed — AT-HYG `bayer` or `flam` is non-empty","bit6 (0x40)":"absmag-missing — AT-HYG `absmag` was empty (derive it from mag + distance instead)","bit7 (0x80)":"ci-from-hyg — AT-HYG had no colour index, so it was back-filled from HYG v4.1 (bit4 is then clear)"}},"source":"AT-HYG v4.0 — AT-HYG database, Astronomy Nexus (David Nash)","sourceUrl":"https://codeberg.org/astronexus/athyg","sourceFile":"data/subsets/athyg_40_reduced_m10.csv.gz","downloadUrl":"https://codeberg.org/astronexus/athyg/media/commit/eebe42b3552ae04e67d27ae085a8aad997b42bc0/data/subsets/athyg_40_reduced_m10.csv.gz","sourceVersion":"AT-HYG v4.0 @ commit eebe42b3552ae04e67d27ae085a8aad997b42bc0","retrieved":"2026-10-14","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Star data: AT-HYG v4.0 database, Astronomy Nexus (David Nash), CC BY-SA 4.0","frame":"ICRS equatorial, right-handed cartesian; +x towards (RA 0h, Dec 0), +z towards Dec +90","epoch":"J2000.0 — positions are AT-HYG x0/y0/z0, the epoch-2000 cartesian columns, used verbatim","units":"parsecs","secondarySources":[{"name":"HYG v4.1 — variability and multiplicity flags, joined on HIP then HD","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/astronexus/HYG-Database/3bf37f4b2d5460e1278286320d1d62fab9b493c1/hyg/CURRENT/hygdata_v41.csv","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"name":"Stellarium v26.3 skycultures/modern_iau — constellation figures","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Stellarium/stellarium/v26.3/skycultures/modern_iau/index.json","licence":"GPL-2.0-or-later (code) / CC BY-SA 4.0 (skyculture data)"},{"name":"NASA Exoplanet Archive pscomppars (TAP sync) — exoplanet host flag","url":"https://exoplanetarchive.ipac.caltech.edu/TAP/sync?query=select%20pl_name%2Chostname%2Chd_name%2Chip_name%2Cgaia_dr3_id%2Csy_pnum%2Cra%2Cdec%2Csy_vmag%20from%20pscomppars&format=csv","licence":"Public domain (NASA Exoplanet Archive, NASA/Caltech)"}],"alignment":"Each chunk block starts on a 2-byte boundary so its int16 fields can be read in place; a chunk with an odd record count is followed by one pad byte. Chunk blocks are otherwise byte-identical to the per-pixel files they replace.","chunkLayout":"chunks[].byteOffset is the start of that pixel block within l2.bin; the block is 9 * count bytes and its internal field offsets are relative to byteOffset."}